# The Sphinx protects "instant and sorcery spells you control" and nothing else (CR 101.2, 701.5a). Same turn 1 as the instant scenario.
# Turn 3: Bot1 casts Ponder (a sorcery, paid with the Island) and Bot2's Counterspell (Island and Mox Sapphire) targets it: the Ponder
# resolves - Bot1 puts the Ornithopter on top and draws it. Turn 5: that Ornithopter, a creature spell, is countered by Bot2's second
# Counterspell, the positive control that the Counterspells work with the Sphinx in play (the Ornithopter ends in Bot1's graveyard).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Island
Sphinx of the Final Word
Ponder
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Counterspell
Island
Island x20

